From 2681ca09cdcad798f89a636ce0e2dd673e1cb99f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:07:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] GPU fixes: review (ILUT, test margins, documentation)

- HypreILU: option `HypreILUType` (type of the factorisation of hypre).
  The ILUT factorisations work when hypre computes on a GPU, where the
  ILU(k) factorisations with a level of fill greater than zero fail: the
  refusal of these levels names ILUT, and a level of fill is refused for
  an ILUT factorisation. The failure is reproduced with hypre 3.2.0, not
  3.0.2 as written before.
- HypreILUTest: variant on one process, where the levels of fill change
  the numbers of iterations more than on two; the default level of fill
  on the host (the one of MFEM) and ILUT are checked.
- FixedPointSolverTest: the number of iterations of Crossed2Deltabis,
  which depends on the roundings up to a factor two (from 240 to 562 on
  the host), is no longer bounded; on a GPU, the other bounds are
  increased by two iterations instead of 50%, their numbers of iterations
  differing by at most one from the ones on the host.
- The cached shape functions are only checked by their number of points,
  their number of degrees of freedom being the one of the element.
- Documentation: `isHypreUsingGPU` (only `MFEM_USE_MPI` guards
  `mfem::HypreUsingGPU`), `MFEM_DEVICE` (takes precedence over
  `MFEM_MGIS_DEVICE`), the stale references to the unknowns given by
  `MakeTRef` (with or without prolongation), and the kernels run in the
  Debug and Coverage builds.
